1
00:00:01,656 --> 00:00:03,083
Hi freestylers!

2
00:00:03,267 --> 00:00:07,693
Today, as nobody could have guessed,
it's a "manipulations" tutorial!

3
00:00:07,777 --> 00:00:17,565
[Music]

4
00:00:17,649 --> 00:00:19,013
Step one!

5
00:00:19,097 --> 00:00:32,932
[Music]

6
00:00:33,016 --> 00:00:38,020
First, a fairly simple "manipulation",
called the "frame rotation".

7
00:00:41,043 --> 00:00:43,256
Quick note:
this video is mirrored for right-handers.

8
00:00:43,340 --> 00:00:46,005
(since I'm right-handed,
simple as that).

9
00:00:46,043 --> 00:00:48,338
Sorry, lefties,
but since you already struggle enough

10
00:00:48,422 --> 00:00:50,100
in this world,
I can send you a flipped version

11
00:00:50,184 --> 00:00:51,367
of the video, just ask.

12
00:00:52,576 --> 00:00:57,021
To start learning this one,
begin from this position,

13
00:00:57,212 --> 00:01:01,147
with the frame resting
on your weak hand, my left one.

14
00:01:02,783 --> 00:01:07,146
Then do the same, starting
from the other hand, and catch the frame

15
00:01:07,230 --> 00:01:11,372
with your second hand, and repeat.

16
00:01:11,883 --> 00:01:15,303
This gets you used to the weight
and rotation of your unicycle

17
00:01:15,387 --> 00:01:17,952
without the risk of catching
your fingers in the frame.

18
00:01:18,749 --> 00:01:23,113
As you get more confident,
you can put your hand straight on the tire

19
00:01:23,197 --> 00:01:27,956
and use the spin's momentum
to do a full turn every time.

20
00:01:28,456 --> 00:01:32,883
Ideally, the wheel doesn't move
thanks to your abs and titan arms.

21
00:01:33,253 --> 00:01:36,347
At first, though,
a slight, almost circular movement helps.

22
00:01:37,985 --> 00:01:39,485
Variation 1.

23
00:01:39,836 --> 00:01:43,553
Here's the trick at full speed.
Now let's break it down.

24
00:01:44,556 --> 00:01:47,870
First, you stop the frame
on your second hand.

25
00:01:48,253 --> 00:01:51,278
The saddle's weight
pulls the frame down.

26
00:01:51,416 --> 00:01:54,740
Then cross your second hand

27
00:01:54,824 --> 00:01:56,925
over the one already there.

28
00:01:57,189 --> 00:01:59,756
It acts as a relay
to free up your first hand,

29
00:01:59,840 --> 00:02:02,812
which then catches the tire
once the frame has gone past.

30
00:02:03,243 --> 00:02:08,354
You can break the trick down
this way before doing it at full speed.

31
00:02:11,583 --> 00:02:16,064
To avoid smashing the hand
that stops the frame,

32
00:02:16,148 --> 00:02:21,033
make a slight downward movement
with your hands to slow it down.

33
00:02:22,036 --> 00:02:24,123
And for the smoothest flow,

34
00:02:24,207 --> 00:02:28,740
the "relay" hand should move
into place as early as you can.

35
00:02:31,090 --> 00:02:32,517
Variation 2.

36
00:02:32,627 --> 00:02:36,405
This one adds a half-turn of the unicycle
to the "frame rotation" manipulation.

37
00:02:37,129 --> 00:02:40,040
The spin comes from your second arm
(the right one for me),

38
00:02:40,124 --> 00:02:43,056
just as your first hand
lets go of the tire.

39
00:02:43,882 --> 00:02:45,835
That hand grabs the tire right away

40
00:02:45,919 --> 00:02:48,947
so the other hand can come back
the right way round.

41
00:02:50,369 --> 00:02:55,429
It's a combined outward rotation
of the forearm, wrist and shoulder,

42
00:02:55,513 --> 00:02:58,533
which only works if you drop your hand
diagonally to the left.

43
00:02:58,617 --> 00:03:04,479
[Music]

44
00:03:04,563 --> 00:03:06,472
So my right hand passes it

45
00:03:06,556 --> 00:03:10,693
to my left hand,
tracing a half-circle downward.

46
00:03:12,509 --> 00:03:13,064
There you go!

47
00:03:13,088 --> 00:03:15,405
The great thing about "manipulations"
is that anyone can do them.

48
00:03:15,783 --> 00:03:18,436
Obviously, it's easier
with a light unicycle.

49
00:03:19,343 --> 00:03:20,939
After that, invent...

50
00:03:21,536 --> 00:03:23,765
Why am I putting on a southern accent?

51
00:03:24,716 --> 00:03:28,620
Then invent new variations
and combine them.

52
00:03:28,704 --> 00:03:37,219
[Music]

53
00:03:37,303 --> 00:03:39,703
I hope this video helped.

54
00:03:39,960 --> 00:03:42,056
Post your questions,

55
00:03:42,140 --> 00:03:46,600
your progress and your likes
in the comments. See you!

56
00:03:50,643 --> 00:03:52,720
Oh yeah! I still had battery left!

57
00:03:52,804 --> 00:04:04,497
[Music]

58
00:04:04,581 --> 00:04:06,035
I hope that made sense...

59
00:04:07,329 --> 00:04:09,016
Not sure I covered everything...

60
00:04:13,483 --> 00:04:15,020
Damn! How do I stop this?

